{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "id": "PAPER-paper-method-add-008",
  "track": "paper",
  "title": "Opening the black box toward a modular approach to spike sorting",
  "status": "source_unresolved",
  "objective": "surpass_source_paper_same_task",
  "goal": "Surpass the source-paper result on the same task: Recover individual unit spike trains from simulated extracellular recordings and exceed the source end-to-end sorter accuracy results under the original static and drifting conditions. This binds an actually evaluated task in the same paper, not a new proxy endpoint.",
  "primary_outputs": [
    "Candidate method and outputs for the source task: Recover individual unit spike trains from simulated extracellular recordings and exceed the source end-to-end sorter accuracy results under the original static and drifting conditions. This binds an actually evaluated task in the same paper, not a new proxy endpoint.",
    "Source-paper comparison for Original main Figure7 ground-truth unit-accuracy panel with paired static/drifting conditions and companion unit-error counts; exact scalar or joint panel rule unresolved: Corrected per-ground-truth-unit spike accuracy is TPij/(Ni+Nj−TPij), higher is better. Source figure also reports well-detected, false-positive, redundant and overmerged counts. Exact native matching tolerance, assignment/default thresholds and their publication-version binding still require recovery; the erroneous first-preprint denominator must not be used."
  ],
  "success_criteria": [
    "Recover the exact publication-compatible generator and native evaluator dependencies, full original seed/probe/condition manifest for the predeclared complete source panel, and its published score arrays before admission.",
    "Compare a frozen end-to-end method with the original source methods, including Lupin and the strongest matching comparator, on all recordings of the predeclared original panel with identical scoring and permitted inputs.",
    "Predeclare the exact source-panel claim, meaningful effects, required companion error-count outcomes, aggregation and dependence-aware uncertainty. Retain every source condition within that panel; no favorable SNR, unit, seed or motion subset may define victory after results. A complete main-panel win need not cover unrelated supplementary probes, but must not claim them.",
    "Keep true spike assignments and other oracle component inputs out of end-to-end candidate inference. A perfect-template or true-peak component benchmark cannot replace end-to-end sorting.",
    "Original public-seed performance and any newly protected-seed extension must be reported separately; the extension cannot become a same-task paper win.",
    "The legacy Figure 8 curation/yield/raster implementation remains calibration only and cannot establish simulation accuracy.",
    "The bound improvement contract must be improvement_ready and its complete same-task comparison and admission requirements must pass.",
    "Reproduction is calibration only; reconstructing a numerical result, changing the task or split, or achieving stronger significance alone is not success."
  ],
